mpegts: an interrupt in a packet is no lost packet or cut PES

When the caller's interrupt callback stops a read of the input (with
0099, hls reads a segment on after it), read_packet() got the part of a
TS packet that was read and took it for the end: the bytes were lost,
and the next call resynced on the next sync byte. mpegts_read_packet()
flushed the PES packets it was collecting on that error, so a cut PES
was handed on flagged corrupt ("PES packet size mismatch") and the rest
of it dropped. One interrupt inside an audio PES of an hls TS segment
lost a dozen audio frames and gave a corrupt one; a player that
interrupts the read while paused (to stop prefetching) met it on every
long pause, depending on where the read stood.

When a packet's read comes back short and the input's error is
AVERROR_EXIT, seek back to the packet's start and return AVERROR_EXIT:
the packet is read whole on the next call. The seek is within the I/O
buffer: read_packet() asks the buffer to keep a packet's length before it
reads one (ffio_ensure_seekback(), which moves at most a packet's bytes,
once per buffer), so a packet begun before a refill that brought only
part of its rest is kept too; on a seekable input the seek may go to the
input. Only a DVHS packet (192 bytes) read right after a resync can lose
the 4 bytes before its sync byte that way, and with them the packet
(logged at debug level); 192-byte TS does not occur in hls. On
AVERROR_EXIT, mpegts_read_packet() keeps the PES data read so far and
returns the error; the next call reads on. A stale AVERROR_EXIT in the
error of an input that is not hls already ends avio_read() (hls clears
it once data or the end comes, 0077 and 0112), so other callers see no
change.

diff --git a/libavformat/mpegts.c b/libavformat/mpegts.c
--- a/libavformat/mpegts.c
+++ b/libavformat/mpegts.c
@@ -3182,6 +3182,10 @@ static int read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, uint8_t *buf, int raw_packet_size,
     AVIOContext *pb = s->pb;
     int len;
 
+    /* The packet stays in the buffer until it is read whole, also when a
+     * refill is cut by an interrupt (see below). */
+    ffio_ensure_seekback(pb, raw_packet_size);
+
     // 192 bytes source packet that start with a 4 bytes TP_extra_header
     // followed by 188 bytes of TS packet. The sync byte is at offset 4, so skip
     // the first 4 bytes otherwise we'll end up syncing to the wrong packet.
@@ -3190,6 +3194,16 @@ static int read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, uint8_t *buf, int raw_packet_size,
 
     for (;;) {
         len = ffio_read_indirect(pb, buf, TS_PACKET_SIZE, data);
+        if (len != TS_PACKET_SIZE && pb->error == AVERROR_EXIT) {
+            /* The caller's interrupt callback cut the packet: back to its
+             * start (the bytes are still in the buffer), so that it is read
+             * whole on the next call. After a resync the 4 bytes before a
+             * DVHS packet's sync byte may be gone; that packet is lost. */
+            int back = FFMAX(len, 0) + (raw_packet_size == TS_DVHS_PACKET_SIZE ? 4 : 0);
+            if (back && avio_seek(pb, -back, SEEK_CUR) < 0)
+                av_log(s, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "Packet cut by an interrupt not kept\n");
+            return AVERROR_EXIT;
+        }
         if (len != TS_PACKET_SIZE)
             return len < 0 ? len : AVERROR_EOF;
         /* check packet sync byte */
@@ -3198,8 +3212,8 @@ static int read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, uint8_t *buf, int raw_packet_size,
 
             if (mpegts_resync(s, raw_packet_size, *data) < 0)
                 return AVERROR(EAGAIN);
-            else
-                continue;
+            ffio_ensure_seekback(pb, TS_PACKET_SIZE);
+            continue;
         } else {
             break;
         }
@@ -3506,6 +3520,12 @@ static int mpegts_read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, AVPacket *pkt)
     pkt->size = -1;
     ts->pkt = pkt;
     ret = handle_packets(ts, 0);
+    /* An interrupt is no end: the PES data read so far is kept for the next
+     * call, which reads on. */
+    if (ret == AVERROR_EXIT) {
+        av_packet_unref(ts->pkt);
+        return ret;
+    }
     if (ret < 0) {
         av_packet_unref(ts->pkt);
         /* flush pes data left */
